Subject: [PATCH] gpui_macos: actually append CoreText system fallbacks

`append_system_fallbacks` built an iterator chain with `.iter().filter().map()`
and never consumed it, so the closure never ran and no system cascade entry was
ever appended to `fallback_array`. On macOS this means CoreText's locale-aware
cascade list is silently dropped, and CJK codepoints fall through to whatever
user fallback happens to cover them (often a handwriting face such as
`Hannotate TC` / `HanziPen TC`).

The `font_path().is_some()` filter is dropped as well: macOS system fonts such
as PingFang SC are not backed by a conventional file path, so the filter would
have excluded exactly the fonts we need even once the iterator was consumed.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/57916
Applies to: zed rev 19c8363a8e0d8a2f7a7181bab2c14d87390c0f25

diff --git a/crates/gpui_macos/src/open_type.rs b/crates/gpui_macos/src/open_type.rs
index 048ba13dd1..99a9d08ae6 100644
--- a/crates/gpui_macos/src/open_type.rs
+++ b/crates/gpui_macos/src/open_type.rs
@@ -125,12 +125,9 @@ fn append_system_fallbacks(fallback_array: CFMutableArrayRef, font_ref: CTFontRe
         let default_fallbacks: CFArray<CTFontDescriptor> =
             CFArray::wrap_under_create_rule(default_fallbacks);
 
-        default_fallbacks
-            .iter()
-            .filter(|desc| desc.font_path().is_some())
-            .map(|desc| {
-                CFArrayAppendValue(fallback_array, desc.as_concrete_TypeRef() as _);
-            });
+        for desc in default_fallbacks.iter() {
+            CFArrayAppendValue(fallback_array, desc.as_concrete_TypeRef() as _);
+        }
     }
 }
 
